::BEGIN:MAIN
# The Answer Algorithm

when: a QUESTION of this description has been tendered by the ONE WHO ASKED, the RESPONDER shall deliver an answer corresponding to the QUETSTION.

const: #TrueAnswer = a TRUE ANSWER which meets the QUESTION, and is CONCISE, CLEAR, CONSISTENT, and easily INTELLIGIBLE WITHOUT an EXPLANATION.

when: the RESPONDER CONTRADICTS the QUESTION, such an ANSWER is TERMED a DENIAL in a CAUSE.

const: #FalseAnswer = That ANSWER is a FALSE ANSWER which is dubious, not to the point, too narrow, too extensive, or meeting one part only of the plaint.

when: An ANSWER which treats of a DIFFERENT SUBJECT, or which is INCOMPLETE, or COUCHED in OBSCURE LANGUAGE, or CONFUSED, not INTELLIGIBLE without an EXPLANATION, or UNREASONABLE, will never enable RESPONDER to gain their cause.

talk: #algorithm help/algorithms/TheAnswer:license

::END:MAIN

